  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Marketing L P has $857M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The company won 302 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.8M. Obligations fell down 56.4% year over year in the current fiscal-year-to-date snapshot. Historical annual obligations rose from $522M in FY21 to $2B in FY25, with FY26 at $857M so far. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $810M in obligations. The Software Publishers market accounts for $856M of FY2026 to date obligations. Several agencies show smaller activity, including the Social Security Administration at $46.6M and the General Services Administration at $763K. The Department of Homeland Security shows $0 in obligations. This profile shows concentrated demand from defense buyers and a market footprint centered on software publishing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of Dell Marketing L P in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $810M for Dell Marketing L P in FY2026 to date. The Social Security Administration obligated $46.6M and the General Services Administration obligated $763K. Additional buyers with smaller obligations include the District of Columbia Courts at $372K and the Committee for Purchase from People Who Are Blind or Severely Disabled at $150K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Dell Marketing L P federal revenue?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the largest market with $856M in FY2026 to date obligations. Computer and Computer Peripheral Equipment and Software Merchant Wholesalers accounted for $171K and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services accounted for $29.5K. Other listed markets include Sales Financing at $209K and a second Software Publishers entry at $199K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Dell Marketing L P make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Dell Marketing L P has $857M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The firm received 302 awards so far and the average award size is $2.8M. Historical obligations climbed from $522M in FY21 to $2B in FY25, with FY26 at $857M year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Dell Marketing L P?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, having obligated $810M. Other buying agencies include the Social Security Administration at $46.6M, the General Services Administration at $763K, the District of Columbia Courts at $372K, and the Committee for Purchase from People Who Are Blind or Severely Disabled at $150K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Dell Marketing L P sell to the government?",
      "a": "Dell Marketing L P primarily sells software-related offerings, with Software Publishers accounting for $856M in FY2026 to date obligations. Other federal markets include Computer and Computer Peripheral Equipment and Software Merchant Wholesalers at $171K and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $29.5K."
